 xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133599691,imgsize-1859168.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Las Vegas Valley converted 250 million sq ft of lawn to save water, saving 203 billion gallons]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133599635.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Las Vegas is making headlines for its initiative to remove grass lawns, which has successfully conserved billions of gallons of water. Nevertheless, this environmental strategy has led to a concerning increase in local summer land-surface temperatures, soaring by around 20 degrees Celsius. As a response, water agencies are now promoting the use of water-efficient landscaping and shade trees, and new guidelines prevent grass installations in residential yards.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/las-vegas-valley-converted-250-million-sq-ft-of-lawn-to-save-water-saving-203-billion-gallons-researchers-found-turf-removal-can-raise-summer-land-surface-temperatures-about-20c/articleshow/133599635.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/las-vegas-valley-converted-250-million-sq-ft-of-lawn-to-save-water-saving-203-billion-gallons-researchers-found-turf-removal-can-raise-summer-land-surface-temperatures-about-20c/articleshow/133599635.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T01:37:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133599682,imgsize-2058629.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Harmeet Dhillon reacts to Ankit Gupta-YC controversy: American employers cannot discriminate against US citizens]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https: